200.description:
A generic empty message that you can re-use to avoid defining duplicated
empty messages in your APIs. A typical example is to use it as the request
or the response type of an API method. For instance:

    service Foo {
      rpc Bar(google.protobuf.Empty) returns (google.protobuf.Empty);
    }

parameters.description:
Create the named link if absent, applying all supplied mutable state and
ignoring update_mask. Existing links can only be changed by their owner;
an identical desired state returns the existing resource unchanged.
